# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Files that must never reach version control.
#
# Unlike the chat lab, this project holds NO API KEY — it never calls
# Anthropic, so there is no secret to leak here. The .env line below is
# kept anyway, for two reasons: the habit is worth keeping consistent
# across both projects, and a reader who copies this file into a project
# that DOES hold a key should find the protection already in place.
#
# A key committed to a repository is a leaked key even if you delete it in
# a later commit, because the old commit still contains it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Local configuration — never commit these
.env
.env.local

# Installed packages — restore with `npm install` instead
node_modules/

# Compiled output — regenerate with `npm run build`
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# The browser half compiles in place, so its output sits in public/ next to
# the source. Generated, not written by hand — regenerate with
# `npm run build:client`.
public/*.js
public/*.js.map

# shared/ holds types only, so it compiles to an empty module — but the
# client build still emits one next to the source, same as public/.
shared/*.js
shared/*.js.map

# Claude Code
#
# CLAUDE.md IS committed — it is project guidance and belongs in the repo.
# These are the per-developer bits that should not be:
#   settings.local.json  one person's approved-tool choices
#   .claude/*            local session state, scratch files, logs
# A shared .claude/settings.json can be committed by force-adding it
# (`git add -f`) if the project ever wants team-wide Claude settings.
.claude/
.claude/settings.local.json

# Editor and OS clutter
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
